<section class="page-section">
  <div class="shell split">
    <aside class="split__aside">
      <span class="eyebrow">I / Position</span>
      <h2>A closed archive, not an empty one.</h2>
    </aside>
    <div class="split__body" data-reveal>
      <p>
        The internet rewards a full grid. A studio should not. Presenting unfinished
        work as a portfolio creates a false signal: it says the work is done when it is
        not. A-XS keeps the archive closed until a project has earned its page.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is a deliberate constraint, not a placeholder. The work in progress covers
        language design, native systems, and interfaces. When a project is finished, its
        dossier will be published here with the architecture, the measurements, and the
        known limits. Until then, access is by introduction.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        “A disclosed limit is worth more than a hidden one.”
        <cite>A-XS / method</cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

