<section class="page-section">
  <div class="shell split">
    <aside class="split__aside">
      <span class="eyebrow">III / The dossier</span>
      <h2>What a private dossier contains.</h2>
      <p class="mono-label">Enough to evaluate the work, not enough to pad a deck.</p>
    </aside>
    <div class="split__body">
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step" data-reveal>
          <span class="step__num">01</span>
          <h3>Scope.</h3>
          <p>
            The problem, the constraint, and the decision that defined the build. What
            was deliberately left out is part of the record.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="step" data-reveal>
          <span class="step__num">02</span>
          <h3>Architecture.</h3>
          <p>
            The system map: components, boundaries, data flow, and the parts that carry
            the most risk. Diagrams where a diagram is clearer than a paragraph.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="step" data-reveal>
          <span class="step__num">03</span>
          <h3>Measurements.</h3>
          <p>
            What was measured, how, and on what hardware. Results include the failures
            and the gates that were not met. A number without a method is not included.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="step" data-reveal>
          <span class="step__num">04</span>
          <h3>Limits.</h3>
          <p>
            The edge of the current build: unimplemented surfaces, known trade-offs, and
            the next constraint. Stated plainly, before the demo.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="page-section">
  <div class="shell split">
    <aside class="split__aside">
      <span class="eyebrow">IV / Access</span>
      <h2>A short protocol.</h2>
      <p class="mono-label">No form. No funnel. A direct conversation.</p>
    </aside>
    <div class="split__body">
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step" data-reveal>
          <span class="step__num">01</span>
          <h3>Introduction.</h3>
          <p>
            A message through GitHub with who you are and what you are working on. A
            sentence is enough to start.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="step" data-reveal>
          <span class="step__num">02</span>
          <h3>Context.</h3>
          <p>
            The problem, the stage, and why this work is relevant. The more precise the
            question, the more useful the answer.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="step" data-reveal>
          <span class="step__num">03</span>
          <h3>Mutual fit.</h3>
          <p>
            If the work aligns, a dossier is shared under confidence. If it does not,
            the reply will say so directly.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="step" data-reveal>
          <span class="step__num">04</span>
          <h3>Conversation.</h3>
          <p>
            A technical walkthrough, questions, and references. The archive is not a
            pitch; it is evidence.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

